"social_icons_container flexible" style="border-collapse:collapse; padding:15px 0 22px 0">\r\n<table class=social_icons_container_inner cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 border=0 width=229 align=center style="-premailer-cellpadding:0; -premailer-cellspacing:0; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:normal; margin:0 auto; mso-table-lspace:0; mso-table-rspace:0">\r\n<tr>\r\n\r\n<td width=33 class=social_icons_container_inner style="border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 auto"><a href=https://c.gle/AOExmq2Vqe7XAlaqmpvydZvHWdj0yGwoj9M3Olwp4dMbrcOBM9yZmAblWgxXIjwuQfFxcLxua6ywS0r1JFHmaFl8bXERmw4zxWCCh7vfWisWl21_oWoXvcCwmGCDDu4ul8liSy4 target=_blank><img src=http://services.google.com/fh/files/emails/gcp_newsletter_email_blogger.png alt="Visit Google Cloud blog" width=33 style="-ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; border:none; outline:none; text-decoration:none"></a></td>\r\n<td width=16 style=border-collapse:collapse>   </td>\r\n<td width=33 class=social_icons_container_inner style="border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 auto"><a href=https://c.gle/AOExmq3zOF5HJQCVjb7bugBVOXRIZlIuftLEqYm8lTt21qMFCg5uRtKac8jr_WS-uxJYqtAvUCdq3Da5siTQiLMiyiM2rhx9HlmiCWfLelXThsYVcaZbNMCylwY5SIWaejHoq1ljzAO0oFhXU1T4 target=_blank><img src=https://services.google.com/fh/files/emails/gcp_newsletter_email_github.png alt="Visit GCP on GitHub" width=33 style="-ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; border:none; outline:none; text-decoration:none"></a></td>\r\n<td width=16 style=border-collapse:collapse>   </td>\r\n<td width=33 class=social_icons_container_inner style="border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 auto"><a href=https://c.gle/AOExmq0xvbeG_voBUIIRtRgigW-dWnL3YKjOkuSz6gtCYrfFw6jEoFP5rj_GliPztIFZjxHcIbDZv3tpakcHrELHNgJN2-rqCEYst5GbAe1GLLtflRc3rsO2iTR8dz26yyYv9fbPH-IDqnJeEtkjXlK87G8 target=_blank><img src=http://services.google.com/fh/files/emails/gcp_newsletter_email_linkedin.png alt="Visit Google Cloud on LinkedIn" width=33 style="-ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; border:none; outline:none; text-decoration:none"></a></td>\r\n<td width=16 style=border-collapse:collapse>   </td>\r\n<td width=33 class=social_icons_container_inner style="border-collapse:collapse; margin:0 auto"><a href=https://c.gle/AOExmq076365US3LX6opzn9TDUKhFuzX8xUsK8bm6XzQ6CevW86sEK5o1kJ7E02ZF3UQokrK8KvylDUwQ8Sbn_O9yybNxp5R4goSUdJaiMITjEkyf6alHuhex54yuixszEuMb6s5b4yV target=_blank><img src=http://services.google.com/fh/files/emails/gcp_newsletter_email_twitter.png alt="Visit Google Cloud on Twitter" width=33 style="-ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; border:none; outline:none; text-decoration:none"></a></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<div style="display: none; white-space: nowrap; line-height: normal; font-size: 15px; font-weight: normal; font-variant: normal; font-style: normal; font-family: courier; color: #ffffff; width: 480px !important; min-width: 480px !important; max-width: 480px !important;">\r\n                                                                                      \r\n</div>\r\n<img alt="" height=1 width=3 src=https://notifications.google.com/g/img/AOExmq30-eHsIdC_SwGRB22MQ3STJbdcOkYUkIQfAyqCzxvNJ4iZ2Z1reUCkFiJrK2v8ffE51RvDTcbERRLvDw2sQV5ZqBeAp1lJQ54Gmk2mzmUHytT4BwSsnmTGidm2QqC65vIHRQ.gif></body>\r\n</html>\r\n</div>	Review changes to intermediate CAs and TLS certificate types. https://c.gle/AOExmq3uLS0020x1qqPqP0MkIcovclBVKXP5yvfNTzfS7z1Qk71GrqcaJXyJApMkNeWyHMOmtzamMMLP8enwykW9b07mOcFrNWYeA04TH_KG0m-vAQs-p6_i_hn4YfMB3Eg -- \r\n\r\n,\r\n\r\n In Q2 2026, to improve efficiency, we will be updating the Transport Layer Security (TLS) certificate for many Google endpoints. The intermediate Certificate Authority (CA) and certificate type will shift from a RSA certificate chain and leaf certificate to an ECDSA certificate.\r\n\r\n What you need to know\r\n\r\n Key changes:\r\n Many services, including , will shift to using the Google Trust Services WE1 intermediate and ECDSA based TLS certificates.\r\n\r\n Potential impact:\r\n If your client applications are not configured correctly, they may be unable to connect to Google services after this change. Connection failures are most likely to occur in the following two scenarios:\r\n\r\n \r\nCertificate pinning: We do not recommend pinning intermediate or leaf certificates. This practice will cause your application to break during routine certificate rotations. \r\nCustom trust stores: If you use a custom trust store, you must ensure it includes all of Google Trust Services (GTS) Root CAs to prevent outages. \r\n \r\n\r\nFor most customers, no action is required as a result of this change. However, if you run a custom trust store or pin CAs, you may need to take action. We’ve provided additional information to guide you through this change.\r\n\r\n What you need to do\r\n\r\n Action advised before June 15, 2026:\r\n\r\n \r\nEnsure you trust all Google Trust Services Root CAs as detailed in this https://c.gle/AOExmq1Axif4gjFdG6kWX3jtuQ7ypXntKRO-p9Serpxs4nVwxJHmO1m4x37QBmK33mOdzwxzmnEA91P1OnF4AZKCndVVDdobvFgjL6i5JXCv1yDxIPkYqmHPkYCIo4dK8ZNFMziIHTOy_so. \r\nPinning is discouraged. If you choose to pin, ensure that all Google Trust Services Roots and, if applicable, intermediates are in your pin list. \r\n \r\n\r\nTimeline:\r\n Services will shift to new intermediates throughout late Q2 2026.\r\n\r\n Impacted customers/accounts:\r\n Any cloud project using a limited set of trusted roots or pinning certificates may experience issues.\r\n\r\n We’re here to help\r\n\r\n Please review the https://c.gle/AOExmq0oSLXYNK7tNhSDeYC_z54LefpScMayJBZS5ze2y9J7OQI5RZ9jvmz6cTbSxtw0_icw7ReCOqwDTZWGBIkfcwfgzYos2nh-ecQpwzfPv8GBK-oFgGl-imvV8MOHSDUfv9LlxkKDZ5ZkpuKTD_QzQLL-xmxVDkOq6qI for guidance on ensuring reliable connections to Google services.\r\n\r\n If you have any questions or require assistance, please contact https://c.gle/AOExmq2IqXaLWjjO6Xv35PjAwSC5K1o0HI5oMvts38nrGr5ee18skBSVTrQ7NeXpLfhbHH3x44t_SR1mD8Wf3eEEbM9rz8qJBkZBtaFMZLuGaMjJ1qMfbUBSWBk.\r\n\r\n Thanks for choosing Google Cloud.\r\n\r\n — The Google Cloud Team https://c.gle/AOExmq1Axif4gjFdG6kWX3jtuQ7ypXntKRO-p9Serpxs4nVwxJHmO1m4x37QBmK33mOdzwxzmnEA91P1OnF4AZKCndVVDdobvFgjL6i5JXCv1yDxIPkYqmHPkYCIo4dK8ZNFMziIHTOy_so https://c.gle/AOExmq2IqXaLWjjO6Xv35PjAwSC5K1o0HI5oMvts38nrGr5ee18skBSVTrQ7NeXpLfhbHH3x44t_SR1mD8Wf3eEEbM9rz8qJBkZBtaFMZLuGaMjJ1qMfbUBSWBk Was this information helpful? \r\n\r\n https://c.gle/AOExmq1iLgQ-WhbtXLsMSWMaA_svwoMA1nVq94H998ZgQdp2-K7aitBgvex72ytU2g7vqO8EcM_vdJBFRNJ3mW7vcr3Evw-ua_zu5DnwV37ct2nVQTrPyxZ8zD_h4k7wpFrgPVAPM7NgwfUXJUM7TuJ8keUELKdpIOrq-IWmlYhoCoMkjZFOw1Fi0TH58kYdc7HFaZqQtWpgBYO1wXcnzDUASCJF_Dkd5b-mkn3_qLXkwNZOdP4WAPOcrmarlVcphY5OIQ     https://c.gle/AOExmq0Zj2diqW1qTT3yoitbkHuCpujgG5Bi-xJPL6SX0MM8Ulk0uS63nIN7dnPZ6kBjqRGxkfAvn4xWJl6ZowzmyMC5vw1H7ONhoc_XEtmKiA-1cj3PgNf3JRGjsm-NRYrKFBjiceDHCBuLJUlJ1zyOMG-hty7CvdVAFB5kkIfrYQDTWY5dUP6KxHw6GZIgfJS8f-Z1LnH0vElAE1UElWileRaDFs1CJC4fv6BKRzx2DXQjcwvxWVgCu5V_XmuOwbmnUMmBYdk     https://c.gle/AOExmq0jq1Nikd6lx7gE0aBoANJ-kQFmxskMOQCQGZxLlNEYKJTPYYMokXzMJti-_eWJDMKy0czGpHSritb7Qcb9GMZXzzRL11etSdJpRvupZfx1R5D1BrrcilHC8ZWNms1xeS3wTZoW0UTNFMZoqiToUabYM2GtJobqXPUircgTcWie29F3y7cu-O6H-4CpSsoTXvMDUC8AQ_MRk9-J3dglqs1YXPyaiWmzv5nS4hXi8VM9X75y9axG_Fz3-9iLHD8X \r\n\r\n © 2026 Google LLC 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043 \r\n\r\n You’ve received this mandatory service announcement to update you about important changes to Google Cloud or your account. https://c.gle/AOExmq2Vqe7XAlaqmpvydZvHWdj0yGwoj9M3Olwp4dMbrcOBM9yZmAblWgxXIjwuQfFxcLxua6ywS0r1JFHmaFl8bXERmw4zxWCCh7vfWisWl21_oWoXvcCwmGCDDu4ul8liSy4     https://c.gle/AOExmq3zOF5HJQCVjb7bugBVOXRIZlIuftLEqYm8lTt21qMFCg5uRtKac8jr_WS-uxJYqtAvUCdq3Da5siTQiLMiyiM2rhx9HlmiCWfLelXThsYVcaZbNMCylwY5SIWaejHoq1ljzAO0oFhXU1T4     https://c.gle/AOExmq0xvbeG_voBUIIRtRgigW-dWnL3YKjOkuSz6gtCYrfFw6jEoFP5rj_GliPztIFZjxHcIbDZv3tpakcHrELHNgJN2-rqCEYst5GbAe1GLLtflRc3rsO2iTR8dz26yyYv9fbPH-IDqnJeEtkjXlK87G8     https://c.gle/AOExmq076365US3LX6opzn9TDUKhFuzX